# Intentionally empty.
#
# ChromaticFirmwareUpdater refuses to start unless a file with this exact name
# exists in /etc/udev/rules.d (it only checks that the file exists, not what
# it contains). The real rules live in 70-modretro-chromatic.rules, which has
# to sort before 73-seat-late.rules for TAG+="uaccess" to take effect.
